<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Part(ii)
We recursively obtain the <math id="S2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> values of <math id="S2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}=P_{3k+1}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{3k}-v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}=P_{3k+1}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{3k}-v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> as we increase the value of <math id="S2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, let <math id="S2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G_{k})=\zeta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G_{k})=\zeta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to verify that the <math id="S2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="S2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{4}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{1}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{1}=4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>, it is clear that <math id="S2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{2})=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{2})=3</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add <math id="S2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> to each of the <math id="S2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to get <math id="S2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{3},v_{6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{3},v_{6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{3},v_{6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{3},v_{6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, we add <math id="S2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> to each <math id="S2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> that includes <math id="S2.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S2.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. This produces two additional <math id="S2.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets for <math id="S2.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S2.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, with the new and unique set <math id="S2.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5}\}</annotation></semantics></math> which covers all other vertices except <math id="S2.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate two more <math id="S2.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.p12.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> for one and <math id="S2.p12.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> for the other. It is clear that <math id="S2.p12.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p12.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> (and vice-versa), giving <math id="S2.p12.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{6}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{6}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S2.p12.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{2}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{2}=8</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math>, it is also clear that <math id="S2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{3})=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{3})=4</annotation></semantics></math>. We use a very similar construction as in the case when <math id="S2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add <math id="S2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> to each of the <math id="S2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to get
<math id="S2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{3},v_{6},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{3},v_{6},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{6},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{6},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{3},v_{6},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{3},v_{6},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{6},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{6},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{6},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7},v_{9}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{6},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7},v_{9}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
. Further, we add <math id="S2.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> to each <math id="S2.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that includes <math id="S2.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S2.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{8}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p13.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p13.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{9}</annotation></semantics></math>. This produces three additional <math id="S2.p13.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets for <math id="S2.p13.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S2.p13.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7},v_{10}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7},v_{10}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7},v_{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},v_{4},v_{7},v_{10}\},\{v_{2},v_{4},v_{7},v_{10}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{7},v_{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, with the unique set <math id="S2.p13.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8}\}</annotation></semantics></math> which covers all other vertices except <math id="S2.p13.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate two more <math id="S2.p13.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p13.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.p13.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> for one and <math id="S2.p13.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> for the other. Thus, <math id="S2.p13.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.p13.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> (and vice-versa) giving <math id="S2.p13.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8},v_{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8},v_{9}\},\{v_{2},v_{5},v_{8},v_{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S2.p13.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{3}=13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{3}=13</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, we generalize the previous constructions for all <math id="S2.p13.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is obvious that <math id="S2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{k})=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{k})=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. So, for <math id="S2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we repeatedly form the <math id="S2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by extending those of <math id="S2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> covers both <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> to each <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We add <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to each <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> that includes <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the unique set <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> which covers all other vertices of <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> except <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate two more <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> for one and <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the other. Clearly <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (and vice-versa) and we have <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1},v_{3k+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1},v_{3k+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">From steps (a)-(c), we generate a sequence of <math id="S2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> values, with <math id="S2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4,8,13,19,26,34,43,\ldots" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>43</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4,8,13,19,26,34,43,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> let <math id="S2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}=\{S\subseteq V(G_{k})\ |\ S\ \text{is a}\ \gamma-\text{set in}\ G_{k}\ \text{and}\ v_{3k+1}\in S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>is a</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>set in</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}=\{S\subseteq V(G_{k})\ |\ S\ \text{is a}\ \gamma-\text{set in}\ G_{k}\ \text{and}\ v_{3k+1}\in S\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}=\{S\subseteq V(G_{k})\ |\ S\ \text{is a}\ \gamma-\text{set in}\ G_{k}\ \text{and}\ v_{3k+1}\notin S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>is a</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>set in</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}=\{S\subseteq V(G_{k})\ |\ S\ \text{is a}\ \gamma-\text{set in}\ G_{k}\ \text{and}\ v_{3k+1}\notin S\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=|A_{k}|,b_{k}=|B_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=|A_{k}|,b_{k}=|B_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G_{k})=a_{k}+b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G_{k})=a_{k}+b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="S2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in B_{k}\implies v_{3k}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in B_{k}\implies v_{3k}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are <math id="S2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> possibilities, if <math id="S2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1},v_{3k-2}\notin S," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1},v_{3k-2}\notin S,</annotation></semantics></math> in which case <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1}\in S." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1}\in S.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}\in S." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}\in S.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">It is not possible that <math id="S2.p17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{v_{3k-2},v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\subseteq S\in B_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{3k-2},v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\subseteq S\in B_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, because this inclusion would imply that <math id="S2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominating set in <math id="S2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is impossible, since <math id="S2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}|=k-1&lt;\gamma(G_{k-1})=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}|=k-1&lt;\gamma(G_{k-1})=k</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for <math id="S2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint possibilities.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">In case <math id="S2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> we see that <math id="S2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=S\setminus\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominating set in <math id="S2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1=\gamma(P_{3(k-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1=\gamma(P_{3(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, and we know that there is only one such set, <math id="S2.p18.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S^{\prime}=\{v_{j}\ |\ j\equiv 2\pmod{3},2\leq j\leq 3k-4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=\{v_{j}\ |\ j\equiv 2\pmod{3},2\leq j\leq 3k-4\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p19.1" class="ltx_p">In case <math id="S2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k}\}\in A_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k}\}\in A_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, if <math id="S2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\in A_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\in A_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar converses apply to cases <math id="S2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>: in case <math id="S2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique <math id="S2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k-1},v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in case 1, if <math id="S2.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\in B_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\in B_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cup\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cup\{v_{3k}\}\in B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Putting these observations together, we have that <math id="S2.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}=a_{k-1}+b_{k-1}+1\ \ \ (*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.5em;" width="1.5em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}=a_{k-1}+b_{k-1}+1\ \ \ (*)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p20.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>; since each set <math id="S2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0,\ldots,k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0,\ldots,k-1</annotation></semantics></math> must contain at least one vertex of <math id="S2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that each <math id="S2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> contains exactly one vertex of <math id="S2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3r+3}\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3r+3}\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=o\ldots k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=o\ldots k-1</annotation></semantics></math>, for if <math id="S2.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3r+3}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3r+3}\in S</annotation></semantics></math> then, because there cannot be more than <math id="S2.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vertices between consecutive elements of <math id="S2.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, it would follow that <math id="S2.p20.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3s+3}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3s+3}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p20.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>. But then <math id="S2.p20.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sole representative of <math id="S2.p20.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p20.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts the premise that <math id="S2.p20.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.p20.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="S2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k}\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k}\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>, so the sole vertex in <math id="S2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cap T_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cap T_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is either <math id="S2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}=v_{3(k-1)+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}=v_{3(k-1)+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-1}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-1}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3k},</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="S2.p21.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S=\{v_{t}\ |\ t=2\pmod{3},\ 2\leq t\leq 3k-1\}\cup\{v_{3k+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo lspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{v_{t}\ |\ t=2\pmod{3},\ 2\leq t\leq 3k-1\}\cup\{v_{3k+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.p21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}\in A_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus\{v_{3k+1}\}\in A_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>; conversely, if <math id="S2.p21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\in A_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\in A_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k-2}\in S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k-2}\in S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p21.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k-2}\}\in A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\cup\{v_{3k-2}\}\in A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p22.1" class="ltx_p">From the preceding paragraph we conclude that, for <math id="S2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=1+a_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=1+a_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S2.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p23.1" class="ltx_p">From <math id="S2.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that, for <math id="S2.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
