<div id="S2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.6</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k+2</annotation></semantics></math> then no <math id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> includes the vertex <math id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k+2</annotation></semantics></math>. As with any path or cycle, if <math id="S2.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq V(P_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq V(P_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is dominating then <math id="S2.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(P_{n})\setminus S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(P_{n})\setminus S</annotation></semantics></math> cannot contain 3 “consecutive” vertices, <math id="S2.p25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p25.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p25.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for each such <math id="S2.p25.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, each set <math id="S2.p25.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{r}=\{v_{3r+1},v_{3r+2},v_{3r+3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{r}=\{v_{3r+1},v_{3r+2},v_{3r+3}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p25.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0,\ldots,k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0,\ldots,k-1</annotation></semantics></math>, contains at least one vertex of <math id="S2.p25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="S2.p26.1" class="ltx_p">Now suppose that <math id="S2.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, one of <math id="S2.p26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+1},v_{3k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+1},v_{3k+2}</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="S2.p26.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, <math id="S2.p26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3k+2}</annotation></semantics></math> would not be covered. Since <math id="S2.p26.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=3k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=3k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be that each <math id="S2.p26.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> contains exactly one element of <math id="S2.p26.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, if <math id="S2.p26.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.p26.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sole representative of <math id="S2.p26.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p26.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. But then <math id="S2.p26.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not covered by <math id="S2.p26.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a cycle on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, then its dominion is
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G)=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G)=3</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout we obtain <math id="S2.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> from a path <math id="S2.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{n-1}-v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{n-1}-v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by connecting <math id="S2.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S2.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{n-1}-v_{n}-v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}:=v_{1}-v_{2}-\ldots-v_{n-1}-v_{n}-v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2.8</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Every <math id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.7.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">The claim is straightforward from the fact that <math id="S2.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(P_{3k})=\gamma(C_{3k})=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(P_{3k})=\gamma(C_{3k})=k</annotation></semantics></math>, and the fact that any dominating set in <math id="S2.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> will be dominating in <math id="S2.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2.9</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(C_{3k})=\zeta(P_{3k})+2=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(C_{3k})=\zeta(P_{3k})+2=3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all <math id="S2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">The unique <math id="S2.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, is also a <math id="S2.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S2.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the <math id="S2.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> rotations, say, clockwise, of this set by <math id="S2.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> places, are also <math id="S2.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets in <math id="S2.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and are distinct subsets of <math id="S2.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{3k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{3k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further rotations will just duplicate the <math id="S2.p29.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> sets already discovered. Thus, <math id="S2.p29.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(C_{3k})\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(C_{3k})\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and to show equality it suffices to show that any <math id="S2.p29.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set <math id="S2.p29.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of vertices of <math id="S2.p29.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> must be one of these <math id="S2.p29.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S2.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set in <math id="S2.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S2.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then at least two consecutive vertices <math id="S2.p30.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,w\in V(C_{3k})\setminus S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,w\in V(C_{3k})\setminus S</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us rename the vertices around the cycle so that <math id="S2.p30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p30.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since neither <math id="S2.p30.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="S2.p30.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, yet <math id="S2.p30.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominating set in <math id="S2.p30.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be that <math id="S2.p30.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a dominating set in the path <math id="S2.p30.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{3k}:=v_{1}-\ldots-v_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{3k}:=v_{1}-\ldots-v_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S2.p30.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{v_{2},v_{5},\ldots,v_{3k-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which, with respect to any other naming of the consecutive vertices round <math id="S2.p30.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math>, is one of those <math id="S2.p30.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.p30.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets in <math id="S2.p30.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3k}</annotation></semantics></math> already discovered.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows from Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5. ‣ 2 Dominion of Some Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> and Claim <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem9" title="Claim 2.9. ‣ Proof. ‣ 2 Dominion of Some Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2.10</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
</div>
<div id="S2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p34.1" class="ltx_p">The cases when <math id="S2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3k+2</annotation></semantics></math> turn out to be more difficult to establish and perhaps require a novel technique. However, using Lagrange interpolation on some early recurring <math id="S2.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>-values, we present a conjecture.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmconjecture1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_conjecture">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmconjecture1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conjecture 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmconjecture1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a cycle on <math id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, then its dominion is 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G)=\begin{cases}\frac{n^{2}+5n}{6},&amp;\text{if}\ n\equiv 1\pmod{3}\\
n,&amp;\text{if}\ n\equiv 2\pmod{3}.\\
\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G)=\begin{cases}\frac{n^{2}+5n}{6},&amp;\text{if}\ n\equiv 1\pmod{3}\\
n,&amp;\text{if}\ n\equiv 2\pmod{3}.\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmconjecture1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Dominion of Join of Graphs </h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is no obvious comparative bound between <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G)</annotation></semantics></math> because, while the former determines the size of the minimum dominating set, the latter counts such sets. Yet, with the few upcoming results, we establish some relationships between these two parameters, in particular using the <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">join</span> operation. Recall, the join of <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, commonly denoted by <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the graph obtained from the disjoint union of <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by adding all edges between <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any connected graph <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\zeta(G)\leq{n\choose\gamma(G)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\zeta(G)\leq{n\choose\gamma(G)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These trivial bounds follow from the fact that any <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set is some selection from <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> counts such sets of size <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. The lower bound is tight for stars while the upper bound is tight for complete graphs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are two connected graphs with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G_{1}\vee G_{2})\geq|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G_{1}\vee G_{2})\geq|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider any pair <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u,v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u,v\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in V(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in V(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that it is a <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> covers <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The previous argument also establishes that <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, given any two graphs <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are two connected graphs with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1\\
2&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})\geq 2.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1\\
2&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})\geq 2.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math>

<br class="ltx_break">Moreover,

<br class="ltx_break"><math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\begin{cases}\zeta(G_{1})+\zeta(G_{2})+\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=2=\gamma(G_{2})\end{cases}\\
\\
\zeta(G_{1})\hskip 39.74872pt+\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1&lt;\gamma(G_{2})\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=2&lt;\gamma(G_{2})\par\end{cases}\\
\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,\hskip 90.3375pt\ \ \text{if}\ 2&lt;\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2}).\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:3.97em;" width="3.97em"></mspace><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="10.197em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\begin{cases}\zeta(G_{1})+\zeta(G_{2})+\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=2=\gamma(G_{2})\end{cases}\\
\\
\zeta(G_{1})\hskip 39.74872pt+\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=1&lt;\gamma(G_{2})\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,&amp;\text{if}\ \gamma(G_{1})=2&lt;\gamma(G_{2})\par\end{cases}\\
\\
|V(G_{1})|\cdot|V(G_{2})|,\hskip 90.3375pt\ \ \text{if}\ 2&lt;\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2}).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first part of the statement regarding the values of <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">So, we proceed to establish the results in the second part of the statement. Throughout, we denote by <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> any <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. 
<br class="ltx_break">(a)

<br class="ltx_break">Suppose <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the join operation, any vertex <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}\in S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}\in S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> also covers any other vertex <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{2}\in V(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{2}\in V(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Likewise, any vertex <math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{2}\in S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{2}\in S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> also covers any other vertex <math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}\in V(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}\in V(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are any <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets of <math id="S3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, the result follows.

<br class="ltx_break">(b)

<br class="ltx_break">Suppose <math id="S3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})=2=\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})=2=\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is clear that each <math id="S3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set <math id="S3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,</annotation></semantics></math> is also a <math id="S3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>- set of <math id="S3.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, following from <math id="S3.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math>. The result follows the argument presented in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3 Dominion of Join of Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.

<br class="ltx_break">(c)

<br class="ltx_break">Suppose <math id="S3.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})&lt;\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})&lt;\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S3.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\gamma(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=\gamma(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, if <math id="S3.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is also a <math id="S3.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S3.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is not, since its size is greater than 1. Similarly, if <math id="S3.p6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.p6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S3.p6.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> but not <math id="S3.p6.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The result follows from the argument presented in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3 Dominion of Join of Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.

<br class="ltx_break">(d)

<br class="ltx_break">Finally, suppose <math id="S3.p6.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2&lt;\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2&lt;\gamma(G_{1})\leq\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. It must be that <math id="S3.p6.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1}\vee G_{2})=2</annotation></semantics></math>. In which case, neither <math id="S3.p6.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="S3.p6.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.p6.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S3.p6.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}\vee G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}\vee G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The result follows from the argument presented in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2. ‣ 3 Dominion of Join of Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any connected graph <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(\underbrace{G\vee\ldots\vee G}_{r})=r\zeta(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>r</mi></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(\underbrace{G\vee\ldots\vee G}_{r})=r\zeta(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Part (a) of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3 Dominion of Join of Graphs ‣ Dominion of Some Graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (when <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G_{1})=1=\gamma(G_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>), the result follows by induction on <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We note that in the case when <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is clear that <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{G\vee\ldots\vee G}_{r}:=K_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>r</mi></munder><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{G\vee\ldots\vee G}_{r}:=K_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(K_{r})=r=r\zeta(K_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(K_{r})=r=r\zeta(K_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, we present a more general result for the special case when <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=\overline{K_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=\overline{K_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the complement of a complete graph on <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> vertices. Note that <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{K_{m_{1}}}\vee\ldots\vee\overline{K_{m_{k}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∨</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{K_{m_{1}}}\vee\ldots\vee\overline{K_{m_{k}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a complete <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-partite graph often written as <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(m_{1},m_{2},\ldots,m_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(m_{1},m_{2},\ldots,m_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=K(m_{1},m_{2},\ldots,m_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=K(m_{1},m_{2},\ldots,m_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is a complete <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-partite graph with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}\leq m_{2}\leq\ldots\leq m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}\leq m_{2}\leq\ldots\leq m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. For some <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G)=\begin{cases}r&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}=1,\ i=1,\ldots,r\ and\ m_{i}&gt;1,\ r&lt;i\leq k,\\
\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leq i,j\leq r\\
i\neq j\end{subarray}}m_{i}m_{j}\ +&amp;\begin{cases}r&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}=2,\ i=1,\ldots,r\ and\ m_{i}&gt;r,\ r&lt;i\leq k,\\
0&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}&gt;2\ i=1,\ldots,r=k.\end{cases}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>r</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>r</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G)=\begin{cases}r&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}=1,\ i=1,\ldots,r\ and\ m_{i}&gt;1,\ r&lt;i\leq k,\\
\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leq i,j\leq r\\
i\neq j\end{subarray}}m_{i}m_{j}\ +&amp;\begin{cases}r&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}=2,\ i=1,\ldots,r\ and\ m_{i}&gt;r,\ r&lt;i\leq k,\\
0&amp;\text{if}\ m_{i}&gt;2\ i=1,\ldots,r=k.\end{cases}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote each disjoint partite (vertex) set of <math id="S3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{i}|=m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{i}|=m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,k</annotation></semantics></math>. If, for some <math id="S3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;r</annotation></semantics></math>, then it is clear that <math id="S3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-sets in <math id="S3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> are the singleton subsets of <math id="S3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}\cup\ldots\cup V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}\cup\ldots\cup V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S3.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(G)=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(G)=r</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,k</annotation></semantics></math>. It is clear that <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(G)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(G)=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Any vertex <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> covers all vertices <math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}\in V(G)\setminus V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}\in V(G)\setminus V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> except those in <math id="S3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for each <math id="S3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}\in V_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}\in V_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v,v^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v,v^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set of <math id="S3.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that there are <math id="S3.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\neq j}^{{k}}m_{i}m_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\neq j}^{{k}}m_{i}m_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> total such sets. Further, if <math id="S3.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{i}|=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{i}|=2</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,r</annotation></semantics></math>, then each such sets, <math id="S3.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, is an additional <math id="S3.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-set, giving the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
